  for the family's sake  aaron moriarty joins us now she's  followed this case for decades and aaron  you were just saying this is the most  vicious case you've ever covered oh  absolutely there were four young women  who were in a yogurt shop you know with  a part-time job who would ever expect  sign and it wasn't just you know that  they were murdered they were shot then  they were piled on top of each other and  they were burned i mean there's nothing  worse and so you know what this case  made me realize that gail and i were  talking about this and i had not thought  about this is the impact on the  investigators we know these families  have lost their loved ones and and they  have to live with that but you don't  think the investigator also and jon  jones there was so much pressure to  solve this murder and he was diagnosed  with ptsd at one point his marriage fell  apart because he was so  single-minded he so much wanted to solve  this he's still holding on to the shirt  that he was wearing well because he  because there have been times when  people have been arrested and convicted  and he always promised the family i will  wear that shirt when i really believe  we've got the killers and he has not put  that shirt on yet what do we know about  that partial dna evidence that you just  mentioned okay this is hopeful so um you  know we hear about genetic genealogy  unfortunately what they have is just  partial so they can't actually put it  into a database yet but there were  recent tests originally the profile had  just 16 markers recent tests were able  to yield 25 markers so there's a hope  that the next set of tests will be able  to do more and maybe lead to the suspect  because i think most people believe  where that dna was  means that that person was involved and  it's going to lead to somebody outside  of the dna is there any other evidence  oh there is this strange clue that has  been just bugging me so much so the  people who are in the yogurt shop  remember two men in their 20s who were  not eating or drinking anything they  seem suspicious to the men they've never  been identified and all the years i've  done stories nobody's ever come forward  and said you know oh i those two guys  may have been and they have no pictures  of them no drawings it's just the phrase  yogurt chop and murders we were saying  those two words just don't go together  and that's right and they shouldn't kids  go it's quite funny  those two words shouldn't go together um  aaron moriarty thank you so much and you  can see aaron's report the yogurt shop  murders tomorrow night at 10 9 central  right here on cbs in the viacom cbs  streaming service paramount plus
 

